Upstream's set_corner_radius/unset_corner_radius handlers are no-op
stubs, so a surface's rounded-corner state changes without ever
triggering a redraw -- the old corners linger on screen until something
else forces a repaint. Force a redraw on both set and unset so corner
radius changes actually render immediately. Confirmed still needed
against 1.5.0 upstream (unrelated to the LayerHookId fix that did land
upstream in ffeda337).

Upstream tried the same fix and reverted it in cosmic-comp#2543,
concluding the redraw "always fails anyway" -- but per their own
investigation in that PR's discussion, it only fails because
visible_output_for_surface() returns None when corner radius is set
before a window's first buffer commit (i.e. on initial window mapping,
the overwhelmingly common case). The redraw genuinely succeeds for the
case this patch actually targets: a live corner-radius change on an
already-mapped window (e.g. changing the theme's rounding at runtime).
Upstream's own maintainer suggested dropping the log message as a
valid alternative to reverting the whole mechanism -- do that instead,
since the warning would otherwise fire on nearly every window creation
(worse than the once-per-boot journald warnings patched out elsewhere
in this tree).

